    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="d355-4" n="4" sameAs="frus:frus1955-57v03mSupp/d355-4"/>

                <head>356. Telegram 1108 from Geneva<anchor n="1" xml:id="d356-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Geneva</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1955-11-09">November 9, 1955, 2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d356-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d356-1"/>
                <p>1108. From Johnson.</p>
                <p>Ekvall informed by M.A. Bern his orders as now amended expire November 26 and
                    cannot under Army regulations be further extended as TDY. On basis info from
                    Defense arrangements would be made between Department and Defense which would
                    permit him bring family to Geneva, Ekvall had made preliminary arrangements with
                    regard to home and personal property and any change at this time will cause him
                    considerable financial loss.</p>
                <p>As Department knows I would be most reluctant be required change interpreters at
                    this time and would not consider it in interest my mission do so. Therefore hope
                    something can promptly be worked out that will enable me retain Ekvall and also
                    resolve his reasonable desire concerning his assignment on an indefinite or long
                    term basis.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Gowen</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
